"<strong>\"A step up transformer makes energy.\"</strong> It raises the voltage only by lowering the current; the power out is never more than the power in.",
"<strong>\"A transformer works on DC.\"</strong> A steady current makes a steady flux, and a steady flux induces nothing.",
"<strong>\"An unloaded transformer draws its full rated current.\"</strong> An ideal one draws none; a real one draws a small magnetizing current that is almost all reactive.",
